8. Explain Replication and Sharding in NoSQL databases
Replication: Copying data across multiple nodes so that the same data exists in more than one place. Provides high availability and read scalability.
Sharding (Partitioning): Splitting data across multiple nodes so that each node holds only a portion of the data. Provides write scalability and capacity growth.
Why important for distributed systems:
Replication → Fault tolerance and high availability (no single point of failure).
Sharding → Horizontal scalability (handle more data and higher throughput by adding nodes).
Together they enable systems that can scale to petabytes and millions of operations per second while remaining available.
